<p>Ukrainian forces launched one of their largest drone attacks on Russia overnight into Sunday, killing at least four people, local Russian authorities said: three in the Moscow region and one in the Belgorod region bordering Ukraine. Russia&#x27;s Defense Ministry said air defenses downed 556 drones overnight and into the morning, while reports described a wave of almost 600 drones across Russian regions, Crimea and the Black and Azov seas. Moscow regional Governor Andrei Vorobyov said a woman was killed in Khimki and two men died in Pogorelki, while Belgorod officials said a man was killed after a drone struck a truck. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said at least 12 people were wounded in Moscow, most of them near the entrance to the city&#x27;s oil refinery, and said the refinery&#x27;s &quot;technology&quot; was not damaged. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy confirmed the strikes and described them as a response to recent Russian attacks on Ukrainian cities; Ukrainian authorities said Russian drone strikes overnight wounded eight people in Ukraine.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/5reuThoMVvim7isO_HuLbz4eR4sp1LmWRYfDWDgluIA2Pdck4uAQhY01EjCmddITgxHCSGRgVD-SKKQrYRFff4xMWeF5sQsaAymNbv6OUQ' alt='An apartment building damaged in a Ukrainian drone attack in Krasnogorsk, in the Moscow region, Russia, on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Strategic-site claims: Ukraine&#x27;s Defense Ministry said several strategic facilities in the Moscow region were struck for the first time.</li><li>Scale comparison: RT reported that several major UAV attacks on Moscow in recent months had not exceeded 65 drones before Sunday&#x27;s raid.</li></ul><blockquote>Entirely justified - Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy: Zelenskyy wrote on X that &quot;Ukrainian long-range sanctions reached the Moscow region,&quot; his term for the Moscow-region strikes. (<a href='http://www.euronews